      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Commanders",
        "body": "The draft room has closed, the tape is in the file, and now comes the harder part - turning hope into a roster. <strong>The Commanders are in post-draft mode, with the rookie class now sitting at the center of every depth-chart debate</strong>, because that's where fresh legs and cheap contracts can still swing a season. Washington sits 3rd in the NFC East, 6 games back, with a 1-game win streak tucked into a year that ended before spring ever warmed up; the bigger truth is that the club's work now is less about standings than sorting out whether this class can plug real holes. That means the linemen must look like adults, the defensive backs must tackle like they mean it, and the skill rookies have to earn snaps instead of being dressed up in press-release optimism. The best drafts don't just add bodies - they change the temperature in a building. Washington needs that kind of jolt. <strong>Watch how quickly the first-year players force their way into the rotation during offseason work, because that will tell you whether this was a tidy draft or a meaningful one</strong>.",
